#: ../../source/docs/common-fpv-first-person-view.rst:5
#: abdf0d5f57814124a61affb157d27897
msgid "First Person View (FPV)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-fpv-first-person-view.rst:7
#: f593f4733c8c403381b04717c51c08f6
msgid "*First Person View* provides you with a true pilot's eye view while flying by placing a video camera and transmitter on your vehicle paired with a receiver and either an LCD or goggles on the ground.  An optional OSD (On Screen Display) helps maintain orientation by providing aircraft instrument overlay on your FPV monitor."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-fpv-first-person-view.rst:17
#: e339c1c0c3104be2ba89cd63a21a0980
msgid "Recommended parts"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-fpv-first-person-view.rst:19
#: 019a3c447a2a4d59bf26ef5e3a794879
msgid "To set up an FPV system on your Copter/Plane equipped vehicle you will need:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-fpv-first-person-view.rst:22
#: 4999b0f4337145309fd88962b8f68737
msgid "Miniature video camera. The variety of cameras increases daily. Most now support resolutions of 600-1200 TVL (TV Lines) and have wide supply range tolerance (5-24V typically). Lens are available from wide-angle (<2.8mm) to ultra-narrow (>5mm). For mini-quads, usually wide angle are used, while for planes, normal field of view/focal lengths (2.8mm-3.6mm) are usually used. A wide selection are easily found by searching the internet for ``FPV Camera``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-fpv-first-person-view.rst:23
#: 9e82f95617dd4c6abaca955259a84e72
msgid "5.8Ghz 25mw to 200mw video transmitter/receiver pair. Again, supply voltage tolerances now easily accommodate 2s-4s Lipo batteries normally used as vehicle power."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-fpv-first-person-view.rst:24
#: 1131685ba67647628285c8de3a5243cf
msgid "OSD (On-Screen-Display). Many autopilots now integrate this function directly. If not, external OSDs like `MinimOSD <http://www.holybro.com/product/micro-osd-v2/>`__ can be used. Or, not used at all. However, being able to see the battery status, flight data, etc. makes a much more enjoyable flight!"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-fpv-first-person-view.rst:25
#: 6de90eda75d84ed4a9b1bd9c36452a53
msgid "Separate batteries for powering the above are rarely needed now, since most now accommodate the flight pack's voltage range from full to empty,"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-fpv-first-person-view.rst:27
#: e98c5ea7f0424ff195001b597164d2b0
msgid "In addition you will need a monitor like the `Black Pearl <http://www.amazon.com/FlySight-Black-Pearl-Diversity-Integrated/dp/B00KR69WHY>`__ or goggles."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-fpv-first-person-view.rst:30
#: efe8b71c9d1149d4bd78f058372de031
msgid "**Goggle options:**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-fpv-first-person-view.rst:32
#: d482cafe66e2489c8445314faad4c01a
msgid "`Fat Shark <http://www.fatshark.com/default.html>`__ has a wide range of goggles including the \"Attitude\" and \"Dominator\" that have been proven to work.  Note that some models come with a built in transmitter & receiver that would replace the 3DR video kits 5.8 Ghz transmitter/receiver pair mentioned above. SkyZone, Eachine, and others also make many models for FPV use."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-fpv-first-person-view.rst:37
#: 4a0bfeb0eddd41e78dcf816860fcfb1b
msgid "Low cost 320x240 resolution goggles (`example video <https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=tG-4JNpE2fc>`__) are not recommended because the higher resolution 640x480 (`example video <https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ywqacXyjcNw>`__) or SVGA goggles provide a much better flying experience."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-fpv-first-person-view.rst:41
#: edca4fc5514e4f6582958325c4a3f481
msgid "In addition you may wish to set-up a separate :ref:`camera gimbal <common-cameras-and-gimbals>`\\ (perhaps with Go-Pro attached) to record the flight in HD."
msgstr ""

